      "card_ref": "EV-PHY-11-MIP-09-009",
      "independent_solution": [
        "Uniform circular motion, R = 0.80 m, frequency nu = 14/25 = 0.56 rev/s -> omega = 2 pi nu = 3.52 rad/s.",
        "a_c = omega^2 R = (3.52)^2 x 0.80 = 9.91 m/s^2.",
        "Constant speed, so the acceleration is centripetal: along the string (radius) towards the centre at every point."
      ],
      "independent_answer": "9.9 m/s^2, along the radius towards the centre",
      "official_answer": "9.9 m/s^2, along the radius at every point towards the centre",
      "agrees": true,
      "numeric_check": "(2*pi*14/25)**2*0.80"
    },
    {
      "card_ref": "EV-PHY-11-MIP-09-011",
      "independent_solution": [
        "v = 900 km/h = 900 x 1000/3600 = 250 m/s; R = 1000 m.",
        "a_c = v^2/R = 62500/1000 = 62.5 m/s^2; a_c/g = 62.5/9.8 = 6.4, so a_c is about 6.4 g."
      ],
      "independent_answer": "about 6.4 g (62.5 m/s^2)",
      "official_answer": "6.4 g",
      "agrees": true,
      "numeric_check": "(900*1000/3600)**2/1000/9.8"
    },
    {
      "card_ref": "EV-PHY-11-MIP-09-013",
      "independent_solution": [
        "(a) If the speed changes there is a tangential component dv/dt besides v^2/R, so the net acceleration is not radial: false (true only for uniform circular motion).",
        "(b) Velocity is the limit of delta r/delta t, which lies along the tangent: true.",
        "(c) Average acceleration over one cycle = [v(T) - v(0)]/T = 0 because the velocity returns to its initial value: true."
      ],
      "independent_answer": "(a) False; (b) True; (c) True",
      "official_answer": "(a) False (true only for uniform circular motion) (b) True, (c) True",
      "agrees": true
    },
    {
      "card_ref": "EV-PHY-11-MIP-09-015",
      "independent_solution": [
        "(a) Uniform circular motion has constant speed: true. (b) Velocity is tangent to the circle, hence perpendicular to the radius vector: true.",
        "(c) Acceleration always points to the centre, so its direction rotates with the particle: true.",
        "(d) Angular momentum about the centre L = m v R, perpendicular to the plane, is constant in magnitude and direction: false. Answer (a), (b), (c)."
      ],
      "independent_answer": "(a), (b), (c)",
      "official_answer": "(a), (b), (c)",
      "agrees": true
    }
  ],
